<h2>Asobi Review 1.0 (build 1615) <span class="when">Oct 15, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed: a RED clip copied without its first file wasn&#8217;t found as a camera original.</b> Asobi only took a clip&#8217;s <code>_001.R3D</code> to stand for it. Now each RED file is found by its own name (the cut can name <code>_004</code>), and the first file there is stands for the clip.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 1476) <span class="when">Oct 12, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>DPX sequences play.</b> 8, 10, 12 and 16-bit DPX files open and play like any other image sequence, read as the color space set for DPX in Settings, Color.</li>
<li>A tall floating Playlist with thumbnails could stop the app. Fixed.</li>
<li>Small fixes.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1441) <span class="when">Oct 11, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Network is in the Review menu.</b> Review ▸ Network; it was under Window. It is also in the right-click Review menu.</li>
<li><b>A playlist on a network drive no longer slows the window.</b> Whether each clip's file is there is checked in the background.</li>
<li><b>Locate Media… reads a folder in the background.</b> A line above the toolbar says how far it has got.</li>
</ul>
